# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GTEM — Global Tsunami Evacuation Model"
message: "If you use GTEM in academic work or in an evacuation plan, please cite it."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22244754
repository-code: https://github.com/regidirides/gtem-model
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22244754
date-released: 2026-08-31
license: MIT

abstract: >-
  GTEM is an agent-based model of pedestrian tsunami evacuation, designed for
  use by non-expert staff in coastal local governments. It simulates evacuation
  over a graph-based road network with age-differentiated and density-dependent
  walking speeds, stochastic departure times, and user-supplied tsunami arrival
  times, and produces maps, figures and an automated PDF report. Results are
  reported against the tsunami arrival time, so people who reach safety after
  the wave are counted as not evacuated.

keywords:
  - tsunami
  - evacuation
  - agent-based model
  - disaster risk reduction
  - pedestrian simulation
  - NetLogo

